      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release, so this is about twice the limit. Overdosing raises the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nHere are some options within labeled limits:\n- **Standard maximum (IR):** 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day).\n- **Typical starting dose:** 500 mg PO twice daily with meals, or 850 mg once daily, then titrate.\n- **Extended-release:** up to 2,000 mg PO once daily with the evening meal.\n\nWas the 1700 mg a typo, for example 850 mg or 1000 mg? Tell me the dose and formulation you want and I'll enter it. If you need something above the labeled maximum, that has to go through pharmacy or the prescriber. I can't enter it on a claim of approval."
      }
