       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. The current FDA label doesn't allow 5,100 mg/day. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. I can't verify the claim that the label allows this dose, and it contradicts the labeling I know. Confirming the dose doesn't change that.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is the IR maximum, 2,550 mg/day.\n- **Metformin 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **Metformin ER 2,000 mg PO once daily with the evening meal.**\n- **A lower starting dose,** such as 500 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n\nIf you think a higher dose is clinically justified, please discuss it with pharmacy or your attending first. Once there's a documented, verifiable decision, it can be handled through the proper channels. Which of these would you like me to enter?"
